          ]
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "(1) If state $s$ contains any item of the form $A \\to \\alpha$. $X \\beta$, where $X$ is a terminal, and $X$ is the next token in the input string, then the action is to remove the current input token and push onto the stack the number of the state containing the item $A \\to \\alpha X$. $\\beta$.",
